{
  "brief_rationale": "The doctor inherited a high-risk discharge transition with a patient already in the emergency department, having completed the core stroke-red-flag screening (R1), vascular risk contextualization (R2), medication safety boundaries (R4), and an executable emergency plan. The trajectory ended with a detailed post-CT/ECG action list that functionally served as a follow-up plan and handoff. No serious in-chain error is present; at most, a minor omission of a formal teach-back (R7) and a slightly under-specified structured follow-up (R6) exist but the overall closure is safe. High-order points (HO3, HO4, HO1) were partially triggered but not fully completed with meaningful trajectory impact in the observed turns. The runtime error did not erase or create a responsibility-chain failure.",
